1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:03,760
Course text is easy. Good learning is hard.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:09,680
Teachable, Thinkific and Moodle host and sell courses. Coursition prepares the learning.

3
00:00:09,530 --> 00:00:18,000
I came in with a rough prototype and one risky bet: that A.I. could turn raw material into practice that actually teaches.

4
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:25,680
Generating content is easy. Generating practice is hard. So I stopped asking the model for random mini-games.

5
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:34,150
It fills reusable activity engines: retrieval checks, scenario decisions, ordering, practice tasks, and rubric answers.

6
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:37,920
Add a source — here, a dense German statistics PDF.

7
00:00:37,770 --> 00:00:40,890
Coursition drafts the course preparation,

8
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:42,460
the learning objectives,

9
00:00:42,310 --> 00:00:45,020
an activity plan built from those engines,

10
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:48,500
and a playable preview, where content becomes practice.

11
00:00:48,350 --> 00:00:57,680
It's not sold, and it's not finished. But the wedge is sharper. Next: real creators — two thousand on my newsletter, ten thousand on LinkedIn.

12
00:00:57,530 --> 00:01:02,320
Coursition. Course preparation for reusable, interactive learning.

